\fs28 \cf2 \cb5 You\'92re right. My earlier same-day reconstruction was too narrow. The voicemail itself does not establish that \'93got upgraded\'94 happened before, during, or immediately after the Venice strike.\cb1 \
\cb5 A stronger reconstruction is that Grandma called during a later weather update:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Lightning hit Venice.\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cb5 Venice looks good on the map.\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cb5 [The storm/forecast/warning] got upgraded.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa165\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 That fits the historical sequence. The July 27 storm continued into July 28, but then weakened. A renewed monsoonal episode reached Southern California on August 2\'963\'97only one week after the deadly Venice event, while it was still fresh in public memory. On August 2, the National Weather Service issued a\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mesonet.agron.iastate.edu/p.php?pid=201408022038-KLOX-WGUS66-FFALOX"}}{\fldrslt 
\f1 \cf7 \cb1 \strokec7 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf7 {{\NeXTGraphic favicon.ico \width580 \height440 \appleattachmentpadding0 \appleembedtype0 \appleaqc
}¬}\
{{\NeXTGraphic favicons.png \width640 \height480 \appleattachmentpadding0 \appleembedtype0 \appleaqc
}¬}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa165\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb5 Flash Flood Watch}}\'a0for parts of Los Angeles County. On August 3, conditions were effectively upgraded to a\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mesonet.agron.iastate.edu/p.php?pid=201408032207-KLOX-WGUS56-FFWLOX"}}{\fldrslt 
\f1 \cf7 \cb1 \strokec7 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf7 {{\NeXTGraphic favicon.ico \width580 \height440 \appleattachmentpadding0 \appleembedtype0 \appleaqc
}¬}\
{{\NeXTGraphic favicons.png \width640 \height480 \appleattachmentpadding0 \appleembedtype0 \appleaqc
}¬}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa165\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb5 Flash Flood Warning}}\'a0as heavy thunderstorms produced flooding and debris flows.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa165\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 Crucially, that warning covered the eastern San Gabriel Mountains\'97not Venice or the Santa Monica coast. The coastal forecast only carried a modest thunderstorm chance. Therefore, Grandma could have been looking at a regional television map and concluding that Venice itself \'93looks good,\'94 even though the wider Los Angeles-area threat had just been upgraded from a watch to a warning.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa150\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 I would now frame it this way:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\b \cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Likely audio:
\f0\b0 \'a0\'93Lightning hit Venice. Venice looks good on the map. Got upgraded.\'94\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\b \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Plausible historical setting:
\f0\b0 \'a0a call between July 27 and August 3, during continuing or renewed monsoonal weather\'97not necessarily on the strike date.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\b \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Strong candidate for \'93upgraded\'94:
\f0\b0 \'a0a forecast, watch, or warning level elsewhere in the region.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\b \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Not established:
\f0\b0 \'a0the exact date of the voicemail or precisely what was upgraded.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 The MP3 contains only a 2021 Logic Pro export date, not the original voicemail date, so the recording itself cannot currently choose between July 27, the following few days, or the August 2\'963 flooding episode. The safest conclusion is that the lightning reference and the upgrade need not describe the same moment\'97and probably should not be forced into one.\cb1 \
